G2532.def:
**καί**,
_conj._,
**and**
I. Copulative.
1. Connecting single words;
(a) **in general**: [[Mat.2.18; 16.1|Mat.2:18, 16:1]], [[Mrk.2.15|Mrk.2:15]], [[Luk.8.15|Luk.8:15]], [[Heb.1.1|Heb.1:1]], al. mult.; repeated before each of the terms in a series, [[Mat.23.23|Mat.23:23]], [[Luk.14.21|Luk.14:21]], [[Rom.7.12; 9.4|Rom.7:12, 9:4]], al.
(b) **connecting numerals **(WM, §37, 4): [[Jhn.2.20|Jhn.2:20]], [[Act.13.20|Act.13:20]];
(with) **joining terms which are not mutually exclusive, as the part with the whole**: [[Mat.8.33; 26.59|Mat.8:33, 26:59]], [[Mrk.16.17|Mrk.16:17]], [[Act.5.29|Act.5:29]], al.
2. **Connecting clauses and sentences**: [[Mat.3.12|Mat.3:12]], [[Act.5.21|Act.5:21]], al. mult.; esp.
(a) **where, after the simplicity of the popular language, sentences are paratactically joined **(WM, §60, 3; M, _Pr._, 12; Deiss., _LAE_, 128ff.): [[Mat.1.21; 7.25|Mat.1:21, 7:25]], [[Mrk.9.5|Mrk.9:5]], [[Jhn.10.3|Jhn.10:3]], al.;
(b) **joining affirmative to negative sentences**: [[Luk.3.14|Luk.3:14]], [[Jhn.4.11|Jhn.4:11]], IIIJhn.10;
(with) consecutive, **and so**: [[Mat.5.1; 23.32|Mat.5:1, 23:32]], [[Heb.3.19|Heb.3:19]], al.; after imperatives, [[Mat.4.19|Mat.4:19]], [[Luk.7.7|Luk.7:7]], al.;
(d) = καίτοι, **and yet**: [[Mat.3.14; 6.26|Mat.3:14, 6:26]], [[Mrk.12.12|Mrk.12:12]], [[Luk.18.7|Luk.18:7]] (Field, _Notes_, 72), [[1Co.5.2|1Co.5:2]], al.;
(e) beginning an apodosis (= Heb. וְ; so sometimes δέ in cl.), **then**: [[Luk.2.21; 7.12|Luk.2:21, 7:12]], [[Act.1.10|Act.1:10]]; beginning a question (WM, §53, 3a): [[Mrk.10.26|Mrk.10:26]], [[Luk.10.29|Luk.10:29]], [[Jhn.9.36|Jhn.9:36]].
3. Epexegetic, **and, and indeed, namely** (WM, §53, 3c): [[Luk.3.18|Luk.3:18]], [[Jhn.1.16|Jhn.1:16]], [[Act.23.6|Act.23:6]], [[Rom.1.5|Rom.1:5]], [[1Co.3.5|1Co.3:5]], al.
4. **In transition**: [[Mat.4.23|Mat.4:23]], [[Mrk.5.1, 21|Mrk.5:1, 21]], [[Jhn.1.19|Jhn.1:19]], al.; so, Hebraistically, καὶ ἐγένετο (וַי:הִי; also ἐγένετο δέ), [[Mrk.1.9|Mrk.1:9]] (cf. [[Luk.5.1|Luk.5:1]] V. Burton, §§357-60; M, _Pr._, 14, 16).
5. καὶ . . . καί, **both . . . and** (for τε . . . καί, see: τε);
(a) **connecting single words**: [[Mat.10.28|Mat.10:28]], [[Mrk.4.41|Mrk.4:41]], [[Rom.11.33|Rom.11:33]], al.;
(b) **clauses and sentences**: [[Mrk.9.13|Mrk.9:13]], [[Jhn.7.28|Jhn.7:28]], [[1Co.1.22|1Co.1:22]], al.
II. Adjunctive, **also, even, still**: [[Mat.5.39, 40|Mat.5:39, 40]]; [[Mrk.2.28|Mrk.2:28]], al. mult.; esp. with pron., adv., etc., [[Mat.20.4|Mat.20:4]], [[Jhn.7.47|Jhn.7:47]], al; ὡς κ., [[Act.11.17|Act.11:17]] καθὼς κ., [[Rom.15.7|Rom.15:7]] οὑτω κ., [[Rom.6.11|Rom.6:11]] διὸ κ., [[Luk.1.35|Luk.1:35]] ὁ κ. (Deiss., _BS_, 313ff.), [[Act.13.9|Act.13:9]] pleonastically, μετὰ κ.. (Bl., §77, 7; Deiss., _BS_, 265f,), [[Php.4.3|Php.4:3]] τί κ., [[1Co.15.29|1 Co 15:29]]; ἀλλὰ κ., [[Luke.14.22|Luk.14:22]], [[Jhn.5.18|Jhn.5:18]], al.; καίγε (M, _Pr._, 230; Burton, §437), [[Act.17.27|Act.17:27]] καίπερ, [[Heb.5.8|Heb.5:8]] κ. ἐάν, see: ἐάν.
**ἐάν**, contr. fr. εἰ ἄν,
_conditional particle_,
representing something as "under certain circumstances actual or liable to happen," but not so definitely expected as in the case of εἰ with ind. (Bl., §65, 4; cf. [[Jhn.13.17|Jhn.13:17]], [[1Co.7.36|1Co.7:36]]), **if haply, if**;
1. with subjc. (cl.);
(a) pres.: [[Mat.6.22|Mat.6:22]], [[Luk.10.6|Luk.10:6]], [[Jhn.7.17|Jhn.7:17]], [[Rom.2.25, 26|Rom.2:25, 26]] al.;
{ (b) aor. (= Lat. fut. pf.): [[Mat.4.9; 16.26|Mat.4:9 16:26]] (cf. ptcp. in [[Luk.9.25|Luk.9:25]] M, _Pr._, 230), [[Mrk.3.24|Mrk.3:24]], [[Luk.14.34|Luk.14:34]], [[Jhn.5.43|Jhn.5:43]], [[Rom.7.2|Rom.7:2]], al.; = cl. εἰ, with opt., [[Jhn.9.22; 11.57|Jhn.9:22 11:57]], [[Act.9.2|Act.9:2]]; as Heb. אִם = ὅταν, [[Jhn.12.32; 14.3|Jhn.12:32 14:3]], I [[Jhn.2.28; 3.2|Jhn.2:28 3:2]], [[Heb.3.7|Heb.3:7]]" (LXX) .
2. C. indic, (as in late writers, fr. Arist. on; see WH, _App._, 171; VD, _MGr._ 2, _App._, §77; Deiss., _BS_, 201f., _LAE_, 155, 254; M, _Pr._, 168, 187; Bl., §65, 4);
(a) fut.: [[Mat.18.19|Mat.18:19]] T, [[Luk.19.40|Luk.19:40]], [[Act.7.7|Act.7:7]]
(b) pres.: [[1Th.3.8|1Th.3:8]] (see Milligan, in l.).
3. **With other particles**: ἐ. καί (Bl., §65, 6), [[Gal.6.1|Gal.6:1]] ἐ. μή (M, _Pr._, 185, 187; Bl., l.with), with subjc. pres., [[Mat.10.13|Mat.10:13]], [[1Co.8.8|1Co.8:8]], [[Jas.2.17|Jas.2:17]], [[1Jn.3.21|1Jn.3:21]] aor., [[Mat.6.15|Mat.6:15]], [[Mrk.3.27|Mrk.3:27]], [[Jhn.3.3|Jhn.3:3]], [[Rom.10.15|Rom.10:15]], [[Gal.1.8; 2.16|Gal.1:8 2:16]] (see Lft., Ellic., in ll.); ἐ. τε . . . ἐ. τε, [in LXX for אִם . . . אִם, [[Est.19.13|Est.19:13]], al.,] [[Rom.14.8|Rom.14:8]].
4. = cl. ἄν (which see) after relat. pronouns and adverbs (Tdf., _Pr._, 96; WH, _App._, 173; M, _Pr._, 42f.; Bl., §26, 4; Mayser, 152f.; Deiss., _BS_, 202ff.): ὃς ἐ., [[Mat.5.19|Mat.5:19]], [[Mrk.6.22, 23|Mrk.6:22, 23]] [[Luk.17.32|Luk.17:32]], [[1Co.6.18|1Co.6:18]], al.; ὅπου ἐ., [[Mat.8.19|Mat.8:19]] ὁσάκις ἐ., [[Rev.11.6|Rev.11:6]] οὗ ἐ., [[1Co.16.6|1Co.16:6]] καθὸ ἐ., [[2Co.8.12|2Co.8:12]] ὅστις ἐ., [[Gal.5.10|Gal.5:10]]
(AS)

G2596.def:
**κατά** (bef. a vowel κατ᾽, καθ᾽; on the frequently neglect of elision, see Tdf., _Pr._, 95; WH, _App._, 146a),
_prep. with genitive, accusative, _
**down, downwards**.
I. C. genitive (WM, §47, k; Bl., §42, 2).
1. C. genitive of thing(s), in local sense;
(a) **down, down from**: [[Mat.8.32|Mat.8:32]], [[Mrk.5.13|Mrk.5:13]], [[Luk.8.33|Luk.8:33]], [[1Co.11.4|1Co.11:4]];
(b) **throughout** (late usage; Bl, l.with): κ. ὅλης κ.τ.λ., [[Luk.4.14; 23.5|Luk.4:14 23:5]], [[Act.9.31; 10.37|Act.9:31 10:37]];
(with) **in a peculiar adjectival phrase**: ἡ κ. βάθους, deep or extreme poverty, [[2Co.8.2|2Co.8:2]]
2. C. genitive of person(s), usually in hostile sense;
(a) **against** (in cl. only after verbs of speaking, witnessing, etc.): opposite to ὑπέρ, [[Mrk.9.40|Mrk.9:40]] μετά, [[Mat.12.30|Mat.12:30]] after ἐπιθυμεῖν, [[Gal.5.17|Gal.5:17]] λαλεῖν, [[Act.6.13|Act.6:13]] διδάσκειν, [[Act.21.28|Act.21:28]] ψεύδεσθαι, [[Jas.3.14|Jas.3:14]] after verbs of accusing, etc., [[Mat.5.23|Mat.5:23]], [[Luk.23.14|Luk.23:14]], [[Rom.8.33|Rom.8:33]], al.; verbs of fighting, prevailing, etc., [[Mat.10.35|Mat.10:35]], [[Act.14.2|Act.14:2]], [[1Co.4.6|1Co.4:6]], al.;
(b) of swearing, **by**: όμνυμι κ. (BL, §34, 1), [[Heb.6.13,16|He 6:13,16]], cf. [[Mat.26.63|Mat.26:63]]
II. C. accusative (WM, §49d; BL, §42, 2).
1. **Of motion or direction**;
(a) **through, throughout**: [[Luk.8.39; 9.6; 10.4|Luk.8:39 9:6 10:4]], [[Act.8.1, 36|Act.8:1, 36]] al.;
(b) **to, towards, over against**: [[Luk.10.32|Luk.10:32]] (Field, _Notes_, 62), [[Act.2.1|Act.2:1]]o 16:7, [[Gal.2.11|Gal.2:11]], [[Php.3.14|Php.3:14]], al.;
(with) in adverbial phrases, **at, in, by, of**: κατ᾽ οἶκον, **at home**, [[Act.2.46|Act.2:46]] κατ᾽ ἰδίαν (see: ἴδιος); καθ᾽ ἑαυτόν, [[Act.28.16|Act.28:16]], [[Rom.14.22|Rom.14:22]], [[Jas.2.17|Jas.2:17]]; with pron. of person(s), [[Act.17.28; 18.15|Act.17:28 18:15]], [[Rom.1.15|Rom.1:15]], [[Eph.1.15|Eph.1:15]], al.
2. Of time, **at, during, about**: [[Act.8.26; 12.1; 19.23|Act.8:26 12:1 19:23]], [[Rom.9.9|Rom.9:9]] [[Heb.1.10|Heb.1:10]], al.
3. **Distributive**;
(a) **of place**: κ. τόποὐς, [[Mat.24.7|Mat.24:7]], al.; κ. πόλιν, [[Luk.8.1|Luk.8:1]], 4 al.; κ. ἐκκλησίαν, [[Act.14.23|Act.14:23]]
(b) **of time**: κ. ἔτος, [[Luk.2.41|Luk.2:41]] ἑορτήν, [[Mat.27.15|Mat.27:15]], al.;
(with) of numbers, etc.: καθ᾽ ἕνα πάντες, [[1Co.14.31|1Co.14:31]] (on καθ᾽ εἷς, see: εἷς); κ. ἑκατόν, [[Mrk.6.40|Mrk.6:40]] κ. μέρος, [[Heb.9.5|Heb.9:5]] κ. ὄνομα, [[Jhn.10.3|Jhn.10:3]]
4. Of fitness, reference, conformity, etc.;
(a) **in relation to, concerning**: [[Rom.1.3, 4; 7.22; 9.3, 5|Rom.1:3, 4 7:22 9:3, 5]], [[1Co.12.6; 10.18|1Co.12:6 10:18]], [[Php.1.12|Php.1:12]]; κ. πάντα, [[Act.17.22|Act.17:22]], [[Col.3.20, 22|Col.3:20, 22]] [[Heb.2.17; 4.15|Heb.2:17 4:15]];
(b) **according to, after, like**: [[Mrk.7.5|Mrk.7:5]], [[Luk.2.27, 29|Luk.2:27, 29]] [[Jhn.7.24|Jhn.7:24]] [[Rom.8.4; 14.15|Rom.8:4 14:15]], [[Eph.2.2|Eph.2:2]], [[Col.2.8|Col.2:8]], [[Jas.2.8|Jas.2:8]], al.
III. In composition, κ. denotes,
1. **down, down from** (καταβαίνω), etc.), hence, metaphorically;
(a) **victory or rule over **(καταδουλόω, -κυριεύω, etc.);
(b) "perfective" action (M, _Pr._, 111ff.).
2. **under** (κατακαλύπτω), etc.).
3. **in succession** (καθεξῆς).
4. **after, behind** (καταλείπω).
5. Hostility, **against** (καταλαλέω).
(AS)

G2563.def:
**κάλαμος**, -ου, ὁ
[in LXX chiefly for קָנֶה, [[Isa.42.3|Isa.42:3]], [[Ezk.40.3|Eze.40:3]] ff., al. ;]
**a reed**: [[Mat.11.7; 12.20|Mat.11:7 12:20]]" (LXX) [[Luk.7.24|Luk.7:24]] hence, accusative, to its various uses,
(a) **a reed-pipe, flute**;
(b) a reed-staff, staff (cf. [[2Ki.18.21|4Ki.18:21]], ῥάβδος καλαμίνη): [[Mat.27.29-30, 48|Mat.27:29-30, 48]], [[Mrk.15.19, 36|Mrk.15:19, 36]];
(with) **a measuring reed or rod **(Ez, l.with): [[Rev.11.1; 21.15-16|Rev.11:1 21:15-16]];
(d) **a writing reed, a pen**: [[3Jn.13|III Jn 13]] (cf. Milligan, _NTD_, 9, 7).†
(AS)
